From 63485be9f2af55425b2979a463bedf59129c8ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 04:06:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 099/112] Volume: every gain after the filters moves per
 sample, rounded, the same in sounds, kit rows, kits, audio tracks and the
 song

The volume stage (ModControllableAudio::processReverbSendAndVolume(), dsp/gain_ramp.h) takes one target per side
per block, v17's gain from the params (post-FX volume with the filters' compensation and the kit/track factor,
times the sidechain, times the pan for kits and tracks), and ramps it per sample from where the last block ended,
landing exactly on the target (32.32 steps from a double quotient, no 64-bit division). Knob, automation, cables
and several params at once all only move the target. Moves of more than 6 dB (to or from 0 included) take at least
5 ms (221 samples), across blocks. The reverb send ramps the same way.

The signal times the gain is rounded once with the gain normalised: a Q31 multiplier and a headroom shift s (0 up
to unity gain), vqrdmulh + vqshl, saturating (v17: smmul << 5, truncated to 32 LSBs, about -116 dBFS of error
with a DC bias; now within 0.5 LSB up to unity, 2^(s-1) above: about -152 dBFS). Unity gain returns the input bit
for bit (below 2^30). Sums saturate instead of wrapping.

The sound's pan (before its effects, as in v17) ramps per sample too, rounded; centred it multiplies by nothing, as
before. The master compressor's gain lands exactly on its target per block and multiplies rounded (smmulr with a
normalised multiplier; v17: truncated step and product). Where the song's/kits' filters ramp their gain
compensation themselves, the volume stage and the master compressor start from the last gain as if it had had this
block's compensation (FilterSet::gainRampStart()), so the two ramps don't both move it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
